From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Min Qin <qinmin@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:20:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] [Download] Ignore late FrameHTMLSerializerHandler
 messages

SavePackageSerializationHandler forwarded DidReceiveData() and
Done() unconditionally. A renderer that keeps the
FrameHTMLSerializerHandler pipe open and sends DidReceiveData()
after Done() would have its data appended to the file while the
asynchronous quarantine for that file was already in flight, and a
second Done() would attempt to run a consumed OnceCallback.

Use the consumed done_callback_ as a sentinel: once Done() has been
delivered, drop further DidReceiveData()/Done() calls.

Changes:
- Early return in SavePackageSerializationHandler::DidReceiveData()
  and Done() if done_callback_ is null.
- Add SavePackageSerializationHandlerTest unit tests covering normal
  and post-Done message ordering.

